(2)/(3) See covering_escape_large_multiple_klein.py -- the escape must be a COVERING set
        (multiple of every q in {2..n}); the tight/mediant minimizers are NON-covering
        (THM-523 trivial class) and do not bound the covering-min.

NET: the LARGE-MULTIPLE-FORCED lemma (part 1) is rigorous & general (q-witness, no primality):
     k in ((n-2)/2, n-2], k not in S, M(S)<=n/Phi6  =>  S has a multiple of k that is >= 2k.
